eferred it","+right back. `graph.py` was added to this node's write set to close the gap.","+","+What changed in `graph.py`:","+","+- `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` — `binding_inventory()` plus D16-D23's","+  node bodies (`acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES`); `binding_inventory()`","+  itself is untouched (`test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_","+  this_nodes_wiring` proves this directly, since N30's own tests recompute","+  their expectations from that return value).","+- `full_binding_inventory()` extended one layer further:","+  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` plus N32's workbook bindings.","+- `register_skeleton` now compiles against `unit_repair_binding_inventory()`","+  and calls a new `register_unit_repair_topology(builder)` — additive, called","+  once after `unit_graph.register_unit_path`, wiring the internal D16-D23","+  loop the same way `workbook.register_workbook_path` wires D24-D32.","+  `unit_graph.py` was not edited.","+","+Required proof, all executed against the real compiled graph (not a declared","+table), in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`:","+","+- `test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`","+  — D16-D23 and M06 are members of `compiled.get_graph().nodes`.","+- `test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges` — all six","+  `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows N31 owns (D08/D09/D12/D14/D91 ->","+  D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS, M05 -> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE) are real","+  edges of `compiled_topology(compiled)`.","+- `test_widening_the_bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error` — a fresh","+  `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` compiles cleanly (no","+  `UnitTopologyError`/`GraphBindingError`).","+- `test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_","+  fast_path` — a real episode run through the real compiled graph reaches","+  `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT` with no repair (D16 PASS","+  fast path).","+- `test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_","+  unit` — a seeded `layout_repairable` finding drives a real","+  D17->D18->D19->D20->D21->D13->D14->D16->D22->D23 traversal over the one","+  real compiled graph, ending in a real accepted receipt.","+","+Fresh compiled-graph evidence (node/edge membership, digest) is recorded in","+`results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_topology.txt`.","+","+`workbook.py`, `unit_graph.py`, and D24-D32 were not touched — N32's write.","+","+## P-N31-003 correction (generation 3): two residual `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures closed","+","+Wiring D16-D23 (P-N31-001) inverted the premise of two pre-existing tests in","+`test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, which is now also in this node's write set for","+exactly these two fixes (nothing else in that file was touched):","+","+1. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its own","+   docstring predicted this exact failure: M05's update is no longer","+   unobservable once the M05->D16 edge is a real, wired edge. Rewritten to","+   assert the current, true invariant — M05's update chunk is a real,","+   non-empty stream chunk and its receipt/review are committed — instead of","+   the retired pre-wiring exclusion.","+2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_","+   langgraph` — a real, reproducible LangGraph `stream(stream_mode=","+   \"updates\")` artifact: the chunk for a step whose *next* step's routing","+   raises in the same tick (the second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call routing","+   to the still-deferred `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`) is never","+   yielded, so `result[\"trace\"]`'s `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` count undercounts","+   by exactly one in the exhausted-after-one-unit case. Fixed the test's own","+   assertion to check the real, checkpointed final state directly","+   (`state[\"selected_unit_id\"] is None`, `state[\"cursor\"]","+   [\"accepted_ordinal\"] == 1`) instead of inferring the outcome from that","+   undercounted trace count. `compiled.stream()`'s call/mode and","+   `graph.py`/`unit_graph.py` were not changed to work around this.","+","+`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` now passes 93/93.","+"," ## Owner / retest map"," ","-| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |","+| Owner | Channel | Repair route | First retest node |"," |---|---|---|---|"," | source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |"," | curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |"]},{"oldStart":58,"oldLines":35,"newStart":116,"newLines":32,"lines":[" "," Frozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17"," owns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns","-the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`). An earlier","-draft of this generation checked both bounds in D17, which made","-`test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child` fail (D17 was","-exhausting a case the prompt's own TEST item expects D18 to exhaust) — fixed","-by removing the attempt-bound check from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17","-... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").","+the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`), per spec's","+own row split (\"D17 ... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt","+bound = exhaustion\")."," "," ## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)"," "," Recomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before"," minting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.","-Categories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),","-domain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content","-check set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join","-result, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one","+Catego